# ExpressiveOS

The sources of ExpressiveOS, built from its own repos. Every project in `default.xml` is pinned to a commit, never to a branch head:

- **ExpressiveOS's own repos** (github.com/ExpressiveOS) are forks of the Evolution X repos it started from. Each is at its `expressiveos` branch: the commit of the ExpressiveOS 1.0 builds (tag `eos-1.0-base`) plus ExpressiveOS's changes as commits.
- **LineageOS's and AOSP's projects** are at the commits of the 1.0 builds until an update moves them.

The Git LFS files of `vendor_gms` and `vendor_google_cheetah` are in [ExpressiveOS/blobs](https://github.com/ExpressiveOS/blobs).

# Initialize local repository
```
repo init -u https://github.com/ExpressiveOS/manifest -b expressiveos --git-lfs
```

# Sync up
```
repo sync -c -j4 --no-clone-bundle --no-tags
```

# Build

ExpressiveOS for the Pixel 7 Pro (cheetah) is built with its kit, `expressiveos-cheetah` in [Denson9874-Device-Central](https://github.com/denson9874/Denson9874-Device-Central). The kit's `setup.sh` sets up and syncs the tree, and `tools/eos-images.sh` runs the build.

# Changing a project

1. Commit to the project's `expressiveos` branch in its ExpressiveOS repo. Never rewrite that branch.
2. Move the project's `revision` in `default.xml` to the new commit, and commit that here.

A project the kit has patches for keeps its full history (no `clone-depth`): the kit finds its changes among its commits.

LineageOS and AOSP updates arrive the same way, as a new commit of this manifest.
